Stop [E3005]: #Pre contract failed: positive
  --> tests/ui/runtime_e3005.jet:3
 Why: A `#Pre` (argument claim, checked at entry) or `#Post` (`result` claim, checked before return) condition evaluated false at runtime. `#Pre contract failed: positive` is the clause's own message string. Checked in every build (not a debug/release split).
 Fix: Fix the caller (a failed `#Pre` means an argument violated the function's stated contract) or the function body (a failed `#Post` means it broke its own promise about the result).
